{"id":"coding-what-is-code","title":"Coding: what is code?","subject":"Coding","label":"Coding","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":171,"duration":170.97,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":471,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Everyday puzzle","start":0,"end":15.925},{"id":"explain","title":"What code is","start":15.925,"end":46.485},{"id":"explain2","title":"Translators","start":46.485,"end":63.515},{"id":"example","title":"Tea and greeting","start":63.515,"end":101.585},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":101.585,"end":111.475},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":111.475,"end":121.145},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":121.145,"end":146.865},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap and tip","start":146.865,"end":170.97}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":5.62,"text":"Have you ever followed a recipe exactly and still got the wrong result? I'm Kora.","w":[0.52,0.66,0.84,1.04,1.4,1.48,2.02,2.96,3.14,3.46,3.66,3.8,4.08,5.04,5.26]},{"s":0,"a":5.92,"b":8.96,"text":"A computer has the same problem, but for a different reason.","w":[5.98,6.06,6.54,6.72,6.84,7.08,7.86,8.04,8.22,8.3,8.62]},{"s":0,"a":9.26,"b":13.19,"text":"It follows exact instructions, yet it cannot guess what you meant.","w":[9.32,9.44,9.86,10.28,11.38,11.7,11.84,12.28,12.56,12.72,12.86]},{"s":0,"a":13.49,"b":15.5,"text":"This lesson explains what code is.","w":[13.54,13.8,14.16,14.66,14.86,15.2]},{"s":1,"a":16.35,"b":18.83,"text":"A computer only follows exact instructions.","w":[16.42,16.5,17.1,17.34,17.74,18.12]},{"s":1,"a":19.13,"b":24.4,"text":"A program is a list of instructions written in a programming language, such as Python or JavaScript.","w":[19.2,19.32,19.96,20.1,20.2,20.46,20.58,21.22,21.48,21.58,21.68,22.18,22.92,23.12,23.26,23.7,23.82]},{"s":1,"a":24.7,"b":27.34,"text":"The code people write is called source code.","w":[24.74,24.88,25.16,25.48,26.14,26.3,26.66,27.02]},{"s":1,"a":27.64,"b":31.72,"text":"So a program tells the computer exactly what to do, one step at a time.","w":[27.7,27.88,27.96,28.44,28.7,28.8,29.36,29.88,30.06,30.16,30.88,31.02,31.24,31.32,31.4]},{"s":1,"a":32.02,"b":34.21,"text":"An algorithm is the step by step method.","w":[32.08,32.34,32.92,33.04,33.16,33.46,33.64,33.92]},{"s":1,"a":34.51,"b":38.11,"text":"The code is that method written in a language a computer can process.","w":[34.54,34.7,35.02,35.14,35.36,35.72,36.06,36.18,36.26,36.74,36.82,37.3,37.46]},{"s":1,"a":38.41,"b":40.18,"text":"A bug is a mistake in the code.","w":[38.48,38.56,38.94,39.08,39.14,39.66,39.74,39.86]},{"s":1,"a":40.48,"b":43.23,"text":"Computers are fast and exact, not clever.","w":[40.52,41.14,41.34,41.8,41.94,42.58,42.84]},{"s":1,"a":43.53,"b":46.06,"text":"They do what you wrote, not what you meant.","w":[43.56,43.78,44,44.14,44.3,45.08,45.38,45.54,45.72]},{"s":2,"a":46.91,"b":52.06,"text":"The processor only understands machine code, which is binary, ones and zeros.","w":[46.94,47.08,47.82,48.12,48.74,49.14,49.76,49.96,50.1,51.16,51.38,51.48]},{"s":2,"a":52.36,"b":56.32,"text":"So a translator program turns source code into something the machine can run.","w":[52.42,52.62,52.7,53.28,53.78,54.14,54.46,54.74,54.98,55.3,55.4,55.78,55.98]},{"s":2,"a":56.62,"b":59.87,"text":"A compiler translates the whole program before it runs.","w":[56.68,56.78,57.44,58.02,58.18,58.44,58.96,59.34,59.46]},{"s":2,"a":60.17,"b":63.09,"text":"An interpreter translates and runs it line by line.","w":[60.22,60.34,60.94,61.64,61.82,62.12,62.28,62.56,62.76]},{"s":3,"a":63.94,"b":64.88,"text":"Take making tea.","w":[63.96,64.24,64.56]},{"s":3,"a":65.18,"b":66.55,"text":"First, boil water.","w":[65.2,65.8,66.16]},{"s":3,"a":66.85,"b":69.01,"text":"Next, put a tea bag in a cup.","w":[66.94,67.68,67.88,67.98,68.22,68.54,68.62,68.7]},{"s":3,"a":69.31,"b":70.62,"text":"Then pour the hot water.","w":[69.34,69.68,69.96,70.08,70.3]},{"s":3,"a":70.92,"b":72.26,"text":"Add milk if you want it.","w":[71.06,71.36,71.66,71.74,71.88,72.08]},{"s":3,"a":72.56,"b":74.95,"text":"Stir, then remove the tea bag.","w":[72.68,73.66,73.9,74.3,74.4,74.6]},{"s":3,"a":75.25,"b":76.2,"text":"Order matters.","w":[75.34,75.62]},{"s":3,"a":76.5,"b":81.86,"text":"If you pour water before boiling it, the tea is wrong, even though every instruction was followed.","w":[76.58,76.7,76.9,77.22,77.62,77.94,78.36,78.8,78.94,79.18,79.34,80,80.2,80.5,80.74,81.26,81.44]},{"s":3,"a":82.16,"b":85.22,"text":"Now the same idea as two lines of Python.","w":[82.26,82.74,82.92,83.26,83.8,83.98,84.26,84.6,84.7]},{"s":3,"a":85.52,"b":87.26,"text":"The first line asks for a name.","w":[85.54,85.7,86.02,86.46,86.78,86.94,87.02]},{"s":3,"a":87.56,"b":89.71,"text":"It also stores the answer under a label.","w":[87.64,87.78,88.12,88.44,88.64,89.02,89.24,89.32]},{"s":3,"a":90.01,"b":92.55,"text":"The second line prints a greeting using that name.","w":[90.02,90.18,90.54,90.9,91.22,91.3,91.78,92.02,92.26]},{"s":3,"a":92.85,"b":94.46,"text":"The board shows the real code.","w":[92.88,93.02,93.38,93.7,93.8,94.06]},{"s":3,"a":94.76,"b":101.16,"text":"In plain words, the code says name equals ask for a name, then print hello and the name.","w":[94.82,94.98,95.32,96.1,96.26,96.58,97.12,97.52,98.06,98.3,98.5,98.58,99.3,99.54,99.82,100.6,100.72,100.86]},{"s":4,"a":102.01,"b":102.64,"text":"Quick check.","w":[102.06,102.36]},{"s":4,"a":102.94,"b":108.3,"text":"What do we call the program that turns source code into machine code before the program runs?","w":[103.04,103.22,103.36,103.5,103.72,103.86,104.4,104.56,104.98,105.34,105.66,105.86,106.3,106.94,107.28,107.4,107.86]},{"s":4,"a":108.75,"b":111.05,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[108.8,109.12,109.44,109.58,109.88,110.5,110.68]},{"s":5,"a":111.9,"b":113.25,"text":"The answer is a compiler.","w":[111.94,112.18,112.54,112.64,112.72]},{"s":5,"a":113.55,"b":119.23,"text":"It translates the whole program before it runs, while an interpreter translates and runs it line by line.","w":[113.62,113.76,114.36,114.48,114.7,115.18,115.48,115.58,116.32,116.6,116.68,117.2,117.84,118,118.28,118.44,118.74,118.92]},{"s":5,"a":119.53,"b":120.72,"text":"Well done if you got it.","w":[119.58,119.84,120.12,120.22,120.36,120.56]},{"s":6,"a":121.57,"b":122.71,"text":"Three common mistakes.","w":[121.6,121.88,122.2]},{"s":6,"a":123.01,"b":125.66,"text":"First, thinking you must be brilliant at maths.","w":[123.1,123.82,124.12,124.26,124.44,124.6,125.1,125.22]},{"s":6,"a":125.96,"b":130.54,"text":"Coding needs clear thinking more than advanced maths, so practise simple problems.","w":[126.02,126.36,126.64,126.9,127.3,127.5,127.66,128.08,128.88,129.1,129.6,129.94]},{"s":6,"a":130.84,"b":133.88,"text":"Second, thinking the computer will guess what you meant.","w":[130.98,131.8,132.12,132.24,132.68,132.9,133.22,133.38,133.56]},{"s":6,"a":134.18,"b":134.89,"text":"It will not.","w":[134.2,134.3,134.52]},{"s":6,"a":135.19,"b":136.78,"text":"It does exactly what you wrote.","w":[135.22,135.34,135.6,136.1,136.24,136.38]},{"s":6,"a":137.08,"b":139.49,"text":"Third, trying to memorise instead of practise.","w":[137.14,137.56,137.88,138,138.52,138.82,138.92]},{"s":6,"a":139.79,"b":142.13,"text":"Write small programs often and test them.","w":[139.82,140.16,140.5,141.16,141.54,141.68,141.94]},{"s":6,"a":142.43,"b":146.44,"text":"The fix is to type small examples yourself instead of rereading notes.","w":[142.48,142.66,143.04,143.14,143.3,143.62,144,144.5,145.1,145.42,145.54,146]},{"s":7,"a":147.29,"b":147.75,"text":"Recap.","w":[147.34]},{"s":7,"a":148.05,"b":151.38,"text":"Code is exact instructions written in a programming language.","w":[148.12,148.42,148.58,149.04,149.74,150.18,150.28,150.38,150.88]},{"s":7,"a":151.68,"b":155.74,"text":"A compiler or interpreter turns source code into something the machine can run.","w":[151.74,151.82,152.5,152.64,153.22,153.58,153.92,154.18,154.42,154.76,154.88,155.3,155.5]},{"s":7,"a":156.04,"b":159.27,"text":"An algorithm is the method, and a bug is a mistake.","w":[156.1,156.36,156.96,157.08,157.24,158.14,158.26,158.38,158.68,158.8,158.88]},{"s":7,"a":159.57,"b":164.61,"text":"Top tip: practise small programs daily, and read your code aloud to check the order.","w":[159.58,159.88,160.58,161.06,161.34,161.88,162.6,162.78,163,163.18,163.42,163.8,163.94,164.18,164.32]},{"s":7,"a":164.91,"b":167.78,"text":"Start with one small task, then change it.","w":[165.02,165.32,165.58,165.76,166.04,167.04,167.26,167.62]},{"s":7,"a":168.08,"b":170.37,"text":"Knowzone is here to help you keep building.","w":[168.2,168.76,168.88,169.1,169.24,169.48,169.66,169.94]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Everyday puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Followed a recipe exactly but wrong result?"},{"at":5.82,"kind":"text","text":"Computers have same problem, different reason"},{"at":9.16,"kind":"text","text":"Exact instructions, cannot guess meaning"},{"at":13.39,"kind":"text","text":"What is code?"}]},{"at":16.1,"heading":"What code is","items":[{"at":16.25,"kind":"term","text":"Computer","detail":"Follows exact instructions only"},{"at":19.03,"kind":"term","text":"Program","detail":"List of instructions in a programming language"},{"at":24.6,"kind":"term","text":"Source code","detail":"Code people write"},{"at":27.54,"kind":"text","text":"Program = exact steps for computer"},{"at":31.92,"kind":"term","text":"Algorithm","detail":"Step-by-step method"}]},{"at":34.26,"heading":"Code and bugs","items":[{"at":34.41,"kind":"text","text":"Code = algorithm in a computer language"},{"at":38.31,"kind":"term","text":"Bug","detail":"Mistake in the code"},{"at":40.38,"kind":"text","text":"Computers: fast and exact, not clever"},{"at":43.43,"kind":"text","text":"They do what you wrote, not what you meant"}]},{"at":46.66,"heading":"Translators","items":[{"at":46.81,"kind":"term","text":"Machine code","detail":"Binary: 1s and 0s; processor understands it"},{"at":52.26,"kind":"term","text":"Translator","detail":"Turns source code into machine-runnable code"},{"at":56.52,"kind":"term","text":"Compiler","detail":"Translates whole program before it runs"},{"at":60.07,"kind":"term","text":"Interpreter","detail":"Translates and runs line by line"}]},{"at":63.69,"heading":"Tea algorithm","items":[{"at":65.08,"kind":"text","text":"1. Boil water"},{"at":66.75,"kind":"text","text":"2. Put tea bag in cup"},{"at":69.21,"kind":"text","text":"3. Pour hot water"},{"at":70.82,"kind":"text","text":"4. Add milk if wanted"},{"at":72.46,"kind":"text","text":"5. Stir, remove tea bag"}]},{"at":75,"heading":"Order and Python","items":[{"at":75.15,"kind":"text","text":"Order matters"},{"at":76.4,"kind":"text","text":"Water before boiling → wrong tea"},{"at":85.42,"kind":"formula","text":"name = input(\"Name? \")"},{"at":89.91,"kind":"formula","text":"print(\"Hello\", name)"}]},{"at":101.58,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":101.58,"kind":"question","text":"What do we call the program that turns source code into machine code before the program runs?"}]},{"at":111.65,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":111.8,"kind":"term","text":"Compiler","detail":"Translates whole program before it runs"},{"at":113.45,"kind":"text","text":"Interpreter translates and runs line by line"},{"at":119.43,"kind":"text","text":"Well done if you got it"}]},{"at":121.32,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":122.91,"kind":"wrong","text":"Must be brilliant at maths"},{"at":130.74,"kind":"wrong","text":"Computer will guess what you meant"},{"at":136.98,"kind":"wrong","text":"Memorise instead of practise"},{"at":142.33,"kind":"tip","text":"Type small examples yourself; don't just reread notes"}]},{"at":147.04,"heading":"Recap and tip","items":[{"at":147.95,"kind":"text","text":"Code = exact instructions in a programming language"},{"at":151.58,"kind":"text","text":"Compiler/interpreter: make source code runnable"},{"at":155.94,"kind":"text","text":"Algorithm = method; bug = mistake"},{"at":159.47,"kind":"tip","text":"Practise small programs daily; read code aloud to check order"},{"at":164.81,"kind":"text","text":"Start with one small task, then change it"}]}],"check":{"at":111.3,"seconds":10,"question":"What do we call the program that turns source code into machine code before the program runs?","answer":"A compiler."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}